<title>GERMANY: German Dresdner says against delaying EMU.</title>
<headline>German Dresdner says against delaying EMU.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Dresdner Bank AG said on Friday it opposed delaying monetary union and denied market rumours that board member Gerd Haeusler had predicted that a delay would occur.</p>
<p>&quot;Mr Haeusler has not at any time and to anyone predicted an imminent postponement of European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU),&quot; the bank said in a brief statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Moreover the bank declares that it is not in favour of a delay in the introduction of monetary union,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>London traders had said there was speculation in the market that Dresdner was predicting that a decision to delay monetary union was pending.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
